  "term": "neurotensin",
  "definition": "Neurotensin is a biologically active peptide first isolated from the hypothalamus. Evidence indicates it functions as a neurotransmitter in both the central and peripheral nervous systems, and it also has effects on blood pressure and smooth muscle activity in animal studies.",
